phi-transport-ws (0.1.6~git202608211603.5d36625-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The connection is the session. A socket starts unauthenticated and may send
    only the handshake, ping and the auth topics; everything else is refused
    here with "unauthenticated" and never reaches core. The identity passed to
    core comes from the connection, not from the frame.
  * Events go only to authenticated connections. Live channel state used to
    reach anything that could open a socket.
  * Browser origins are checked at the handshake, which is exempt from the
    same-origin policy: loopback always, anything else via allowedOrigins in the
    transport config, everything else answered with 403.
  * Idle connections are closed on the budget core states with the session.
    Pre-auth topics do not extend it, so a keepalive cannot hold a session open.
  * TLS is stated, not implied: this plugin does not terminate it, so exposing
    the endpoint beyond the local host means a reverse proxy in front of it.
 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:03:45 +0200

